{
  "plan_id": "AMFE-DATA-PLAN",
  "version": "0.3.0",
  "purpose": "Automated retrieval plan for the R2 data gate and the REAL_TIME evaluation (protocol v4, D-132). Every series is registered OPEN; retrieval is one series per request, rate-limited, without the FRED API service. Latest files come from the public FRED CSV endpoint. Vintage sets come from the ALFRED download-data form: the planned dates are a dense quarter-end grid 1990-03-31..2026-09-30 (147 dates); each planned date is mapped to the latest ACTUAL ALFRED vintage date at or before it (never a future date), the mapped dates are requested in batches of at most 40 per form POST, and the zipped CSVs are merged into one archive with one column per vintage (vintage_check: no observation later than its vintage date). The R2 gate checks a compact spot-check view of the archive (at most 36 dated columns spanning 1990-2026, at least 18 of them before 2000) because a form request carries a limited number of dates.",
  "rate_limit_seconds": 2.0,
  "user_agent": "AMFE-research/0.1 (+https://github.com/Flumos1/Word-economic-model-)",
